Chapter: QwordProbe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 peek-qword over a byte pattern whose top byte has the high bit set, i.e. a
 negative i64. Bare metal loads eight bytes; the zig plug rebuilds the value
 with multiply-and-add, which traps on overflow.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   let b = __heap-save
   in let adv = __heap-advance 64
   in let e = __buf-write-bytes b 0 [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 255]
   in act
     print-line-uni "wrote 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 FF"
     print-line-uni ("peek-qword answers " & integer-to-text (peek-qword b 0))
   end
  end
